# The corpus case that drove most of the rename work: 2982 edits across 60
# files apply with 0 conflicts, //... rebuilds clean, and a second pass has
# nothing left to do.
#
# It took a long time to get here, and the trail is worth keeping. 18081 errors
# in 52 files originally; 2993 in 36 once colliding renames were skipped; 739 in
# 16 once macro arguments were renamed and unrewritable macro references vetoed
# the rename; 621 in 14 once fields of a class nested in a class template mapped
# back to their pattern; 490 once partial and explicit specializations stopped
# being matched against the primary template; 179 once qualified dependent names
# resolved; green once a new name that is a keyword, a macro, or captured by a
# local at an unqualified use stopped being applied at all.
#
# Every one of those was found here rather than by inspection, which is the
# argument for keeping a real corpus in the loop: the last one, renaming
# OnCallSpec::action_ to action inside WillByDefault(const Action<F>& action),
# rewrote `action_ = action` to `action = action` and would have compiled
# silently had that parameter not been const.
#
# NB: this file is sourced by bash, so values must not contain backticks or $.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=member_snake_case
EXPECT=pass
